    "text": "To determine the total cost of Tom's deck, we need to calculate the cost of each type of card and then sum these costs. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Calculate the cost of the rare cards:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of rare cards} = 19 \\times 1 = 19 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the cost of the uncommon cards:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of uncommon cards} = 11 \\times 0.50 = 5.50 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the cost of the common cards:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of common cards} = 30 \\times 0.25 = 7.50 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n4. Sum the costs of all the cards to find the total cost of the deck:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost} = 19 + 5.50 + 7.50 = 32 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total cost of Tom's deck is \\(\\boxed{32}\\).",
